lcl@meceng.coe.northeastern.edu writes:

>A few questions:
>In memorizing additional copies of spellbooks, should you wait until you
>begin to forget the spell, or are the memorized books cumulative, so that
>you get as many casts total if you read a pile of (the same) spellbooks all
>at once?  

I thought this was a good question, so I went and tested it.  It
appears that the number of castings per book read is cumulative, so
that reading two spellbooks will allow you to cast a spell twice as
many times as you would have been able to had you only read one.

>How does one go about using crystal balls?  [Yes, yes, we all know that one
>(a)pplys them, but beyond that?]  What can (and cannot) one find with them,
>and where?  Also, what benefits does a ring of protection from shape
>changers confer?

Crystal balls will allow you to know the positions of every item of
one particular type on your dungeon level, like a selective potion of
object detection.  Rings of protection from shape changers prevent
chameleons and mimics from mimicing other monsters or items.  Mimics
will automatically chase you when you enter the room, since you can
easily detect them.

